WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.450
- Alright, you don't want to
miss anything on social media

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.890
that can make you smile, alright?

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:04.723
We need smiles.

00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:05.800
Don't worry, I've got you covered.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.380
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.330
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.570
A good Charcuterie Board

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.270
takes more than just laying
out some meats and cheeses.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.640
It's an art form people.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.700
Also, how you say it,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.660
because I was told, I say
it wrong, Charcuterie.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.115
Apparently, it's Charcuterie.

00:00:21.115 --> 00:00:23.180
Some will say Charcuterie, for you.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.110
Tiffany in Brooklyn has mastered the art,

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.590
So when she lost her corporate
job during the pandemic,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.100
she had a light-bulb moment.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.560
Her family is obsessed
with her Charcuterie Boards

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.220
complete without using no meat or cheese,

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.410
locally sourced fruits,
jam, nuts and more.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.230
So, she decided to make her
signature spread in boxes

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.710
and sell them for New Yorkers
to enjoy those delicious,

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.450
and people are literally eating them up.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.283
Get it.

00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:49.270
We know you do.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.390
From Cheese &amp; Things,

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:51.570
let's say hi to Tiffany,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.948
who watches the show on NBC 4 New York.

00:00:54.948 --> 00:00:56.122
What's up?

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.441
(crowd cheering)

00:00:57.441 --> 00:00:58.274
- Hi Kelly

00:00:59.313 --> 00:01:00.146
- [Kelly Clarkson] Hello

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:02.150
So, what made you want to do this?

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:02.983
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:03.816
Good question.

00:01:03.816 --> 00:01:05.450
Thank you so much for having me on.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:09.290
So I lost my job like a lot
of people within the pandemic,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.340
and so, I had a lot of time on my hands.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.930
I needed somewhere to
channel my creativity,

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.700
and so a light bulb went off,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.680
and I said, do your boards.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.630
I come from a very large
West Indian family,

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.010
Jamaican to be exact,

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.870
and so my brother is a trained chef,

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:25.790
and the only thing that he would let me do

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.460
was the Charcuterie Boards.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.200
and so it just came to me,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.030
just put your boards in a box.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.600
We were in the middle of a pandemic,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.850
and it just made total sense.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.070
- It does and you can send
one right on over to my house.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.680
I love a Charcuterie Board.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.920
That was over a year ago though,

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.020
so how is business going right now?

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:44.853
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:46.180
It's been amazing.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.578
It's blowing my mind
to be perfectly honest.

00:01:48.578 --> 00:01:49.411
- Where?

00:01:49.411 --> 00:01:50.480
- It's within New York,

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.160
it's very difficult to social distance,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.630
and so with the idea of
going from board to box,

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.090
we developed a solo box,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.000
and so it's for individual consumption.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.060
And so, as New Yorkers,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.930
we're taking to the streets

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.430
and taking to the parks.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:07.140
They still have that communal aspect,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.967
but still being safe.

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:10.410
And so what's next for me

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.370
is really to just be the edible
arrangements of Charcuterie.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.203
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:15.203 --> 00:02:16.310
It sounds amazing.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:17.770
Thank you, Tiffany.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.420
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.710
It looks so good.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:22.543
That's not all.

00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:23.940
Our season long partner Pilot Pen.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.500
The go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.810
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.370
So they'll be using their G2 gel ink pen

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.210
to write you a check for a $1000.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.362
How's that sound?

00:02:34.362 --> 00:02:35.408
(crowd cheering)

00:02:35.408 --> 00:02:36.410
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.536
Thank you

00:02:37.536 --> 00:02:38.989
- Yes.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:41.339
That will make one hell
of a Charcuterie Board.

